.TH PP 1 "August 2026" "ProtoPeek 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pp \- short executable name for ProtoPeek
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pp
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target ]
.br
.B pp download
.RI [ --output " NAME" ]
.RI [ --sha256 " 64_HEX" ]
.I URL
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pp
is an identical executable entrypoint for
.BR protopeek .
Use the canonical name if another installed program already owns
.BR pp .
.SH DEVELOPMENT DOWNLOAD COMMAND
The current development source, but not stable v0.4.0, adds
.BR "pp download" .
It accepts exactly one absolute HTTP(S) URL without user information, an
optional safe output filename with no directory components, and an optional
exact 64-hexadecimal-character SHA-256 digest. It uses a configured or system
.BR aria2c ;
aria2 is not bundled.
.PP
The one-shot command owns its local engine session instead of attaching to an
already-running ProtoPeek process. It writes progress to standard error and the
completed path to standard output. An interrupt returns status 130 and
preserves partial data plus the aria2 session. See
.BR protopeek (1)
for the complete lifecycle and flag constraints.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR protopeek (1)
